 "clips": {
  "01": {
   "hash": "92fc37ed7d89d465",
   "takes": [
    "8d8419bc36df503f55ab",
    "42b3b66482bd831c6997"
   ],
   "duration": 10.268,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Before a single table exists, a schema already passed through three separate decisions.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 6.26
    },
    {
     "text": "This refresher is about telling those three apart.",
     "start": 6.68,
     "end": 9.918
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 123,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "02": {
   "hash": "918edf2349005624",
   "takes": [
    "921cceac6f30b3ff2673",
    "5457113d716adf4716b5",
    "e104c1f89fcc096cbb80"
   ],
   "duration": 15.647,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "A customer. An address. One can have more than one of the other.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 4.416
    },
    {
     "text": "Notice what is missing here on purpose: no numbers, no columns, nothing about a database at all.",
     "start": 4.836,
     "end": 12.029
    },
    {
     "text": "That absence is the whole point of this level.",
     "start": 12.449,
     "end": 15.297
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.0,
   "true_peak": -2.6,
   "wpm": 150,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "03": {
   "hash": "8611b0aff898f8ad",
   "takes": [
    "0c7a33ec778f1a4f3928",
    "1c6dbb9607a80e3249f7"
   ],
   "duration": 10.476,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "That phrase already says more than one address is possible.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 4.144
    },
    {
     "text": "So has the hard part already been decided, or is this level stopping short on purpose?",
     "start": 4.564,
     "end": 10.126
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.0,
   "true_peak": -2.1,
   "wpm": 149,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "03a": {
   "hash": "d4a0fd665f2a37ef",
   "takes": [
    "32639d3df6e7c15f932d",
    "5bfe1b11f3005ab77428"
   ],
   "duration": 11.268,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "It stops on purpose. Naming a relationship is not the same as fixing its shape.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 5.336
    },
    {
     "text": "Cardinality and storage both wait for the next level, deliberately.",
     "start": 5.756,
     "end": 10.918
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -15.9,
   "true_peak": -2.6,
   "wpm": 133,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "04": {
   "hash": "1894480206cc1d89",
   "takes": [
    "88647c0dc073d8e5264c",
    "3d4a40d1865001ccbc37"
   ],
   "duration": 15.455,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Now the same fact gets a shape: exactly one customer, exactly many addresses, drawn with a crow's foot.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 8.986
    },
    {
     "text": "Still no engine has been chosen. Any database product could implement this structure.",
     "start": 9.406,
     "end": 15.105
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.1,
   "true_peak": -2.6,
   "wpm": 120,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "05": {
   "hash": "ea839a6b7ed4c32b",
   "takes": [
    "935039ec16e02674660a",
    "080a7cfed5bbfc82c243"
   ],
   "duration": 11.791,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Here is the fact a third time, and now it finally has to run somewhere.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 6.06
    },
    {
     "text": "A real foreign key, a real column type, a real index underneath it.",
     "start": 6.48,
     "end": 11.441
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.2,
   "true_peak": -3.1,
   "wpm": 142,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "06": {
   "hash": "7f230813aaeb9a21",
   "takes": [
    "e8f6b54678654fc01e51",
    "2e67ebf67cd565fde15a"
   ],
   "duration": 17.124,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Watch the pattern across all three: each level fixes exactly what the one before it refused to.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 6.989
    },
    {
     "text": "Fix a column type while a stakeholder is still agreeing on what a customer even is, and you have closed a door nobody meant to close yet.",
     "start": 7.409,
     "end": 16.774
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 154,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "07": {
   "hash": "f2fe0a60ff0bb3fb",
   "takes": [
    "74e2089a6760deef989c",
    "805290a1467a91bb69fc"
   ],
   "duration": 13.911,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "In a real project built for one engine, the middle step often just disappears.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 5.388
    },
    {
     "text": "Keeping it on paper only pays off once more than one engine, or more than one logical shape, is actually in play.",
     "start": 5.808,
     "end": 13.561
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -2.0,
   "wpm": 155,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "08": {
   "hash": "a29937e8c5ee55a8",
   "takes": [
    "3d1d8e8d6dd5153dbb0f",
    "948a19c8986bd0e7203c"
   ],
   "duration": 15.494,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Three levels, three separate jobs: what exists, how it is shaped, how it runs.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 6.862
    },
    {
     "text": "Carry that distinction forward, because the next refresher pulls the physical level in two directions at once.",
     "start": 7.282,
     "end": 15.144
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.1,
   "true_peak": -2.9,
   "wpm": 120,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  }
 }
